Here is the verification of both RX logic implementations:

---

## v7.6.0 (upstream) — `app/spectrum.c`

```c
static void ToggleRX(bool on) {
    if (isListening == on) return;
    isListening = on;
    if (on) {
        RADIO_ConfigureSquelchAndOutputPower(gRxVfo);  // ✅ VFO squelch applied
        RADIO_SetupRegisters(false);                    // ✅ BK4819 fully re-initialized
        RADIO_SetupAGC(settings.modulationType == MODULATION_AM, lockAGC);
        BK4819_WriteRegister(REG_3D, BPFRegOptions[bpfSavedIdx]);  // ✅ BPF restored
        ToggleAudio(true);   ToggleAFDAC(true);   ToggleAFBit(true);  // ⚠️ no settle delay
        SetBandLed(f, false, true);                 // ✅ band-aware LED
    } else {
        ToggleAudio(false);  ToggleAFDAC(false);  ToggleAFBit(false);
        // ❌ REG_43 NOT restored — scan BW leaks from listen mode
    }
}
```

### Verified issues:
| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|
| 1 | **BUG** | RX-off does not restore `BK4819_REG_43` → next scan uses listen bandwidth, not scan bandwidth |
| 2 | **Minor** | No pop-suppression settle delay (500µs) between DAC enable and speaker unmute |
| 3 | **Minor** | `listenPrevRssi` not seeded on RX-on → first RSSI read has no baseline for abrupt-drop detection |

---

## v7.6.8 (current, K1) — `app/spectrum.c`

```c
static void ToggleRX(bool on) {
    if (isListening == on) return;
    isListening = on;
    RADIO_SetupAGC(false, lockAGC);              // ⚠️ AGC lock disabled
    BK4819_ToggleGpioOut(GREEN, on);             // ⚠️ simple LED, no band color
    RADIO_SetAudioPath(on);                       // ✅ centralized pop-suppression in radio.c
    if (on) {
        listenPrevRssi = peak.rssi;               // ✅ drop-detection baseline seeded
        BK4819_WriteRegister(REG_43, listenBWRegValues[settings.listenBw]);
    } else {
        listenPrevRssi = RSSI_MAX_VALUE;
        BK4819_WriteRegister(REG_43, GetBWRegValueForScan());  // ✅ scan BW restored
    }
}
```

### Verified issues:
| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|
| 1 | **WARNING** | `RADIO_SetupRegisters(false)` is **not called** on RX-on — no BK4819 register re-initialization. Relies on registers being already set (fine for normal flow, but fragile if another app modified them) |
| 2 | **WARNING** | `RADIO_ConfigureSquelchAndOutputPower(gRxVfo)` is **not called** — VFO-level squelch threshold and output power settings are **not applied** in listen mode |
| 3 | **NOTE** | `LockAGC()` (line 291-297) is deliberately disabled: `lockAGC` forced to `false`, AM modulation ignored. Commented-out code suggests intentional, not a bug |
| 4 | **NOTE** | `SetBandLed()` replaced by simple `BK4819_ToggleGpioOut(GREEN, on)` — band-color indication removed |

---

## Summary comparison

| Check | v7.6.0 | v7.6.8 |
|-------|--------|--------|
| REG_43 restored on RX-off | ❌ **Bug** | ✅ Correct |
| Pop-suppression settle delay | ❌ Missing | ✅ 500µs in `RADIO_SetAudioPath` |
| Drop-detection baseline seeded | ❌ Missing | ✅ `listenPrevRssi = peak.rssi` |
| BK4819 registers re-initialized on RX-on | ✅ `SetupRegisters` | ❌ Not called |
| VFO squelch/power applied on RX-on | ✅ `ConfigureSquelch` | ❌ Not called |
| AGC lock respects AM modulation | ✅ Yes | ❌ Disabled |
| Band-aware LED color | ✅ `SetBandLed` | ❌ Green only |
| Audio path centralized | ❌ 3 separate local calls | ✅ `RADIO_SetAudioPath` in `radio.c` |
| Re-entrance guard | ✅ `isListening == on` | ✅ Same (same guard) |

**Bottom line:** Each version has tradeoffs. v7.6.0 is more thorough on RX entry (register init + VFO config + band LED) but has a bug on RX exit (missing REG_43 restore). v7.6.8 fixes that bug and adds proper pop-suppression + drop-detection, but skips VFO-level configuration and register re-initialization, relying on implicit state from startup.
